post_install() {
    cat <<'EOF'

Lucent is installed. Two steps remain, neither of which the package can do
for you.

1. Start the background service, as your own user -- this needs no root:

       systemctl --user enable --now lucent-daemon

   Lucent also offers a button for this the first time you open it.

2. Reboot, or re-trigger udev:

       sudo udevadm trigger --subsystem-match=hidraw --action=add

   The udev rule was installed and pacman reloaded it, but the permission it
   grants is applied when a device appears. The keyboard is internal and
   never replugged, so it does not get that permission until the next boot.

The daemon is only needed for the Performance and Battery tabs. Lighting goes
through the OpenRazer daemon and works without it.

EOF
}

post_upgrade() {
    cat <<'EOF'

Restart the Lucent background service to pick up this version:

    systemctl --user restart lucent-daemon

EOF
}

pre_remove() {
    systemctl --user --global disable lucent-daemon.service >/dev/null 2>&1 || true
}
